  "question": {
    "text": "If the system of equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>. Has infinitely many solutions, then the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
